Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 2 — Kotlin-Based Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to reverse engineer Android applications written in Kotlin. Kotlin is not simply "Java with better syntax"—its compiler introduces metadata, synthetic methods, coroutine state machines, delegated properties, default argument dispatchers, inline functions, and other transformations that fundamentally change the compiled output. By the end of this section, you should be be able to distinguish handwritten Kotlin logic from compiler-generated infrastructure and reconstruct the developer's original intent.



> Core Principle:
Reverse engineering Kotlin means reverse engineering the Kotlin compiler before reverse engineering the application.




